@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log for when you want raw text. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``.
+
+Unlike print, ``out`` does not pretty print containers, word wrap, crop, interpret markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written literally, so ``[bold]`` and ``:smiley:`` appear as typed. It does apply highlighting (on by default, and can be turned off with ``highlight=False``) and an optional ``style``, which behave as they do for print. Output still goes through the normal print path, so render hooks and the buffer are used as usual.
+
+Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("[not bold] :smiley:", "foo", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+
